   "seed": 4900127
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "pat2",
   "x": 40,
   "y": 1760,
   "width": 824,
   "height": 15,
   "strokeColor": "#94a3b8",
   "text": "[11] Adversarial Role Separation: the no-self-review rule — the role that builds does not grade, and says so first",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false,
   "seed": 4900128
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "pat3",
   "x": 40,
   "y": 1782,
   "width": 882,
   "height": 15,
   "strokeColor": "#94a3b8",
   "text": "[16] The Permission Ladder: the one role that writes has its scope as advice — the lowest rung, where the most is at stake",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false,
   "seed": 4900129
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "proto",
   "x": 40,
   "y": 1818,
   "width": 1127,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#94a3b8",
   "text": "prototype: reads a fabricated definition the way a harness would, checks four attempted writes against the file scope and the grant,\nlays the two overlapping sentences side by side · --narrowed adds the frontmatter line that fixes the grant and nothing else · no model, no build, no writes",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false,
   "seed": 4900130
  }
